          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "মাপা (māpā) is a tadbhava, a word inherited and reshaped by sound change. It comes from māpyate, \"is measured\", a form CDIAL reconstructs from its descendants (CDIAL 10054)."
